
  riscvsim › demo 2 · Waiting for memory
  See why an add must wait one cycle for a load.

   1  # A load reads memory in MEM, one stage later than the
   2  # ALU, so the add right after it must wait one cycle.
   3  .data
   4  value:  .word 41
   5
   6  .text
   7  addi x4, x0, 1     # x4 = 1
   8  lui  x2, 0x10000   # x2 = 0x10000000, where value is
   9  lw   x1, 0(x2)     # x1 = 41, read from memory
  10  add  x3, x1, x4    # needs x1 now: one stall

  cycle 1
    IF addi x4, x0, 1  ID ·  EX ·  MEM ·  WB ·
    › The first instruction, addi, is fetched from memory.

  cycle 2
    IF lui x2, 0x10000  ID addi x4, x0, 1  EX ·  MEM ·  WB ·
    › addi is decoded and reads its source registers.

  cycle 3
    IF lw x1, 0(x2)  ID lui x2, 0x10000  EX addi x4, x0, 1  MEM ·  WB ·
    › addi is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 4
    IF add x3, x1, x4  ID lw x1, 0(x2)  EX lui x2…  MEM addi x4,x0,1  WB ·
    › lui is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 5
    IF ·  ID add x3, x1, x4  EX lw x1, 0(x2)  MEM lui x2…  WB addi x4,x0,1
    ✓ x4 = 1
    ! lw is reading memory. add must wait one cycle because it needs x1 from
      lw.

  cycle 6
    IF ·  ID add x3, x1, x4  EX bubble  MEM lw x1, 0(x2)  WB lui x2, 0x10000
    ✓ x2 = 0x10000000
    › lui finishes and writes x2 = 0x10000000.

  cycle 7
    IF ·  ID ·  EX add x3, x1, x4  MEM bubble  WB lw x1, 0(x2)
    ✓ x1 = 41
    › add needs x1 from lw, so it is forwarded from the MEM/WB latch and
      nobody waits.

  cycle 8
    IF ·  ID ·  EX ·  MEM add x3, x1, x4  WB bubble
    › Nothing is left to fetch, so the pipeline is emptying.

  cycle 9
    IF ·  ID ·  EX ·  MEM ·  WB add x3, x1, x4
    ✓ x3 = 42
    ✓ add writes x3 = 42, and the program is finished.

  ✓ 9 cycles · 4 instructions · CPI 2.25 · 1 stall · 0 mispredictions
    Ends with x4 = 1 · x2 = 0x10000000 · x1 = 41 · x3 = 42
    Why it slowed down:
    • lw is reading memory. add must wait one cycle because it needs x1 from
      lw.

  Next: riscvsim demo 3 (Skipping the wait)